    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) headline our offensive output. **James Wood** is our premier start, boasting an elite 0.420 xwOBA and capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Chandler, where his speed profile against a slow delivery nets a meaningful efficiency boost. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% platoon edge against Mahle, compounded by a park factor boost and a prime #2 lineup slot. **Brice Turang** (75.06) also remains an essential play; his aggressive base-stealing profile against the slow delivery of E-Rod, paired with his leadoff status, provides the high-floor production we prioritize given our league\u2019s premium on stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 50.71. While **Travis Bazzana** carries the benefit of an elite #1 order position, the platoon disadvantage against a left-handed arm like Murphy ultimately stifled his projection enough to keep him on the bench in favor of more efficient platoon-advantage hitters like **Mickey Moniak**. **Austin Riley** was also considered, but his unfavorable matchup against the 3.47 xERA of McLean makes him a clear hold for a better day, as we aim to preserve our game caps.\n\nRisks today are moderate, but managers should watch the defensive mechanics in our stolen base targets. While **James Wood**, **Brice Turang**, and **Zach McKinstry** all receive efficiency bumps for facing pitchers with slow deliveries to the plate, **Corbin Carroll** faces a slight regression in his scoring (72.02) due to an elite hold pitcher potentially stifling his base-path upside. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Isaac Paredes** closely to ensure the late-arriving official lineups do not force a benching shift. We are currently sitting **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** to maintain strict efficiency.",
